## (root)
#c9[i5] Typical context summaries suffer three blind spots: unknown loss, silent rot, and lack of traceability.
  > README.md:7-9 #e4958ca1597e
#c10[i5] HCS provides three core capabilities—Traceable, Verifiable, and Measured—without requiring an LLM for the first two, but measurement needs a model.
  > README.md:15-17 #46c742fb364d
#c11[i3] Installing HCS requires Node.js version 18.17 or higher and has zero runtime dependencies.
  > README.md::Install #c24666a9bbdc
#c12[i4] The compiler reads every text file, respects .gitignore and .hcsignore, and discards any claim or probe whose quoted source is not present.
  > README.md::"1. Compile a context file from your project" #ef515161ea43
#c13[i4] In a sample run, `hcs check` reported 64 claims, 30 probes, with 2 moved claims and 1 stale claim.
  > README.md:22-29 #407bf13fa08e
#c14[i4] `hcs score` outputs fidelity with a 95% bootstrap confidence interval and also reports misled and abstention rates for context and no‑context runs.
  > README.md::"2. Measure it" #05f9e4c17028
#c15[i4] `hcs init` creates an empty file for hand-written claims.
  > README.md::Commands #2893e350bcce
#c16[i3] `hcs validate <f>` performs a syntax check.
  > README.md::Commands #2893e350bcce
#c17[i5] `hcs check <f>` verifies all anchors, certificates and suspect claims (exits 1 on stale/missing).
  > README.md::Commands #2893e350bcce
#c18[i4] `hcs render --decoder` prepends short vendor‑neutral instructions for the decoder prompt.
  > README.md::"Decoder prompt" #eb9c14110845
#c19[i3] `openai` provider uses `OPENAI_API_KEY` and optionally `OPENAI_BASE_URL`.
  > README.md::Commands #2893e350bcce
#c20[i4] When `HTTPS_PROXY` is set, hcs re‑runs itself with Node's `--use-env-proxy` flag (Node ≥ 22.21 or 24.5) so requests go through the proxy; `NO_PROXY` is honored.
  > README.md::Commands #2893e350bcce
#c21[i2] HCS is not lossless; it measures the loss instead of hiding it.
  > README.md::"What HCS is not" #e26393a1e153
#c22[i3] The repository layout includes SPEC.md (normative v0.3), src/, test/, bench/, project.hcs, action.yml and the .github/ directory.
  > README.md::"Repository layout" #17f22e9bc351
#c23[i5] The HCS specification version is 0.3.
  > SPEC.md:1 #e855b8e08802
#c24[i5] An HCS file must begin with a magic line that names its version, e.g., "HCS/0.2".
  > SPEC.md::"1. File structure" #8419e4a65a6d
#c25[i5] A 0.3 reader MUST accept files whose magic line is "HCS/0.1" or "HCS/0.2".
  > SPEC.md::"1. File structure" #8419e4a65a6d
#c26[i4] A probe tagged `known` indicates that models answer it correctly without any context.
  > SPEC.md::"4. Probes" #6ad42d520ab7
#c27[i4] A certificate records scoring runs with fields such as `model`, `judge`, `fidelity`, `ci95`, `baseline`, `informative`, `novel`, `judge-agreement`, `tokens`, `budget`, `digest`, and `date`.
  > SPEC.md::"7. Certificates" #3eff969f8f76

