#c156[i3] walk recursively traverses directories, skipping any sub‑directory named ".git" or "node_modules", and adds each file's path (with forward slashes) to the output array.
  > src/sources.ts::walk #62a8544b7420
#c157[i2] isText inspects up to the first 8192 bytes of a Buffer and returns false if any byte is zero, otherwise true.
  > src/sources.ts::isText #b543fad325a5
#c158[i4] chunkFile splits normalized lines into chunks of at most maxLines (default 250), preferring to end a chunk at a blank line after 60 % of maxLines.
  > src/sources.ts::chunkFile #ffc6242f4452
#c159[i4] locateQuote normalizes whitespace and case, requires the quote to be at least three characters, and returns the 1‑based line range of the quote within a chunk or null if not found.
  > src/sources.ts::locateQuote #f12f16ff2c54
#c160[i5] The function `findEnd` scans up to 2000 lines from a start index, tracking brace depth, parentheses, and semicolons to determine the end of a definition in block, value, or JSON mode, returning the line number and whether a body was opened.
  > src/symbols.ts::findEnd #537b9e9d3841
#c161[i5] The `braceSymbols` function scans lines of a brace language file, uses `codeOnly` to ignore non-code, applies `BRACE_DEFS` regexes to detect definitions, filters out imports and local variables, and uses `findEnd` to set the symbol range.
  > src/symbols.ts::braceSymbols #b0597fd3f215
#c162[i4] The `indentSymbols` function extracts symbols from indentation-sensitive languages by matching a regex, determining the block’s indentation level, extending the block until a line with equal or less indentation, and optionally including preceding decorator lines.
  > src/symbols.ts::indentSymbols #955bf38311b8
#c163[i4] The `BRACE_DEFS` array contains regular expressions that match common definition patterns in brace languages, such as functions, classes, constants, and object members, capturing the identifier name.
  > src/symbols.ts::BRACE_DEFS #98e93eb37253
#c164[i3] The exported `SymbolRange` interface defines a symbol’s qualified name and its 1‑based inclusive start and end line numbers.
  > src/symbols.ts::SymbolRange #dea7c7fce18e
#c165[i3] The `CONTROL` set lists language keywords that should not be treated as definitions when matched by the `BRACE_DEFS` regexes.
  > src/symbols.ts::CONTROL #d6ecb6396141
#c166[i5] markdownSymbols identifies markdown headings outside code fences and returns an array of objects containing the heading text, its level, and the start and end line numbers of the section.
  > src/symbols.ts::markdownSymbols #3c9107298a0d
#c167[i5] listSymbols selects a parsing strategy based on the file language: markdown uses markdownSymbols, python uses indentSymbols with a regex for async def/class, yaml uses indentSymbols with a key regex, and other languages use braceSymbols with flags for JSON and file extensions.
  > src/symbols.ts::listSymbols #20db3769bf48
#c168[i5] listSymbols qualifies symbol names by nesting: the innermost strictly enclosing symbol becomes the parent, producing dot‑separated names such as Parent.Child.
  > src/symbols.ts::listSymbols #20db3769bf48
#c169[i4] findSymbol first returns an exact match; if none, for markdown it performs a case‑insensitive unique match; otherwise it returns a symbol whose name ends with .symbol, or null if ambiguous.
  > src/symbols.ts::findSymbol #7635cce106d5
#c170[i4] enclosingSymbol filters symbols that fully contain the requested line range and are smaller than a configurable maxLines threshold (default 80).
  > src/symbols.ts::enclosingSymbol #c9e2964b3c56
#c171[i4] enclosingSymbol selects the smallest qualifying symbol and verifies that its name resolves back to the same range via findSymbol before returning it, ensuring consistency.
  > src/symbols.ts::enclosingSymbol #c9e2964b3c56
#c172[i3] markdownSymbols toggles a fence flag when encountering lines that start with ``` or ~~~, ensuring headings inside code fences are ignored.
  > src/symbols.ts::markdownSymbols #3c9107298a0d
#c173[i3] In listSymbols, the flat array is sorted by start ascending and end descending to guarantee that outer symbols are processed before inner ones when building the containment stack.
  > src/symbols.ts::listSymbols #20db3769bf48

